 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The parable of 24 is drawn as a worldly garden (rain, growth, wheat, then wind for «أتاها أمرنا»). 25-26 are Paradise: light and geometric moods, no garden, river or dwelling; light for «يدعو إلى دار السلام», footsteps for «صراط مستقيم». Nothing at all is drawn on «وزيادة» (the vision of Allah; both tafsirs). As-Sa'di's «زوج بهيج» (a Quran phrase) is not used. 25's end has no clean cut, so 24-26 is one unit. STAGING v4: c1 (24, the parable of this world) is staged in a garden by day (wither is drawn only in this setting): rain on 24:5 (the water sent down), the ground greens and plants and flowers spring up on 24:9 (mixed with it), people and a camel come on 24:15-16 (what people and livestock eat; a wheat plate for the grains, As-Sa'di); on 24:21 (the land takes its adornment) the camera pans over the crops, no birds; the owners walk into it on 24:23 and the camera closes on them on 24:25 (they think they have power over it, both tafsirs: to harvest it); the camera is wide again from 24:27, so the withering from 24:28 (His command came) is seen over the whole land, not on the men; nobody is hurt and nobody leaves; they lower their heads on 24:34 (As-Sa'di: empty-handed, full of grief) and a falling-leaf plate marks 24:35 (as if it had not flourished). Night or day (24:30-32) is not chosen by any picture beyond the scene's daylight. c2 (25) stays ambient: Allah's call to the abode of peace (Paradise, never drawn); a geometric plate from the Name (25:1); footsteps for the straight path; quiet over 25:1-8. c3 (26) stays ambient on a night sky (no central light) with the background quiet over 26:1-10: nothing at all marks 26:4 (the vision of Allah, both tafsirs). The cover shows the garden in bloom with its owners and the camel (24:22), a garden of this world."
